<font size=5>Minor Maintenance</font>
<br>
<b>Wildlife Habitat Institute (WHI)</b>
<p>
Kurt and Sean removed the erosion control fabric from below water level along the reinforced banks.  Jody Brostrom requested this removal during our TAC meeting/tour.  Jody expressed concern that the coir (coconut) fiber netting located below water surface may act as a smolt trap as water levels decreased.
 
<hr size="2" color=<%=color1%>>

<font size=5>Wetland Delineation Survey</font>
<br>
<b>UI Eco-Hydraulics Group and LRK Communications (LRK)</b>
<p>
Results of the wetland delineation survey were forwarded to Tom Duebendorfer on July 16th.  The following information was sent:
<ul>
<li>24" x 36" plot of survey points with respective labels
<li>11" x 17" plot of survey points with respective labels
<li>11" x 17" plot of wetland, upland and channel polygons
<li>Spreadsheet printout that summarizes the data used to plot the survey points
</ul>
LRK Communications reviewed the draft wetland delineation report from Tom Duebendorfer.  The final report will be sent to the Corps of Engineers in Boise the week of August 10th-14th.  Delineation verification should occur in October

	</td>
	<td width="50%" valign="top">
	
<font size=5>Browse Control</font>
<br>
<b>Wildlife Habitat Institute (WHI)</b>
<p>
Last year we experienced elk chewing and damaging numerous, top-of-bank willow cuttings. This year we applied two gallons of an anti-browse insurance - <i>Treeguard</i> - using a solo backpack sprayer to all the newly planted, easily accessible, willow cuttings. 

<hr size="2" color=<%=color1%>>

<font size=5>Background Data/Literature Search</font>
<br>
<b>UI Eco-Hydraulics Group</b>
<p>
Hourly precipitation data for a weather station located near the Red River Ranger Station was found posted on the Internet by the Western Regional Climate Center.   Precipitation records date back to April 28, 1989 and can be used in the design and modeling of Phase III and IV.
<p>
The literature survey continues for background information that can be used in the design of Phase III and Phase IV, as well as any future extensions of the project beyond the IDFG property. 

<hr size="2" color=<%=color1%>>

<font size=5>Upcoming TAC Field Review/Meeting</font>
<p>
Just a reminder that the combined TAC meeting/Low-flow field review is coming up on September 8th.  A draft agenda will be in the mail in a couple of weeks. 

